    <width>560</width>
    <height>860</height>
   </rect>
  </property>
  <property name="windowTitle">
   <string>Static pipe sizing</string>
  </property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout_main">
   <item>
    <widget class="QTextEdit" name="textEdit_info">
     <property name="readOnly">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
     <property name="maximumSize">
      <size>
       <width>16777215</width>
       <height>190</height>
      </size>
     </property>
     <property name="html">
      <string>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Static pipe sizing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iterative sizing of the pipe dimensions with the dynamic network simulation. Every iteration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;build the network model (pipe bundles of the lines),&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;run the simulation (settings of &lt;i&gt;run simulation&lt;/i&gt;) and load the results,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;flow tracing: mass flow of every customer per line (c_lid) and differential pressure at the substations,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;optional pre-sizing with the specific pressure loss setpoint, then balancing of the customers by reducing pipe dimensions,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the new pipe bundles are written to the lines (missing bundle types are created).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The loop stops when the pipe dimensions do not change anymore, when a state repeats or after the maximal number of iterations. Every pipe is checked against the maximal specific pressure loss at its peak mass flow over the whole simulation period, so lines are not undersized.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version:&lt;/b&gt; either a new child version of the loaded version is created and loaded before the first iteration (the loaded version keeps its pipes), or the pipes of the loaded version are overridden. The mass flows are kept constant within an iteration, the next simulation shows the real effect.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
